    "Actual new small-curvature gauge theorem gives uniformW1,2 and smallL4 local forms. Its radial gauge is used only to make a smooth normal path, with no false radial criticalL4 estimate.",
    "One subsequence for all local forms via Hilbert/Rellich; weaknormal, curvatureweakL2 and ASD passage for Sobolev gauges.",
    "Countable nested extraction on rational overlap balls constructs transition classes; boundedSU2 target preserves group constraint and yields allfiniteLp strong convergence.",
    "First-order transition equation passes strongly inL3; actual critical transition theorem gives full interiorW2,q limit regularity.",
    "Difference drift equation with s=12/5 has forcing tending tozero inLs: formdifferenceL3 timesDhL12 and smallcriticaldrift times matrixdifferenceL6. Actual inverse gives stronggradientL6; globalCZ then strongW2,s convergence.",
    "Sobolev embedding gives uniform convergence on compact overlaps; exact cocycles pass pointwise, giving actual continuous limit bundle data."
  ],
  "precise_scope": "Finite FIXED Euclidean ball cover with given smooth local trivializations and smoothSU2 transition maps for every sequence member; sufficiently small curvatureL2 on each entire ball. Smooth local forms near closed balls.",
